<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Title</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>title</a>   (at your guild master)
</pre>
<p>Players like to have titles for their characters, and there are several ways to 
get one.
</p><p>The first is through your guild. Go to your guild master and type title: you get 
the title of your rank in the guild, like "the dwarf Recruit". As you rise in the 
guild there are new titles; when there is none yet for your level, the guild 
master tells you to come back when you are higher.
</p><p>The second is through a clan. Ask your clan Master or a lord for a title (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Ctitle</a>); depending on the clan's rules you are given one, or asked to do 
a quest for it.
</p><p>Another way is by bribing an administrator for a title (see <a cmd='#'>Help Bribe</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ctitle</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Clan</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Bribe</a>
</pre>




</div>